( 02 / Structured logging and spans) Tj T*
( What, why and how) Tj T*
( event serializes named fields to JSON and records a timestamp. span is a context manager: it) Tj T*
( measures elapsed time and records operation completion or failure. Logs tell what happened,) Tj T*
( metrics tell how often, traces show where. Local timing is not a distributed OpenTelemetry trace.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Practical learning) Tj T*
( Example: authentication 20 ms, embedding 180 ms, retrieval 250 ms, reranking 350 ms,) Tj T*
( generation 1400 ms, evaluation 300 ms = 2500 ms. Identify the bottleneck.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Original source | lines 105-128) Tj T*
(   105 | # ----- 01 Observability: structured events without logging secrets or raw content.) Tj T*
(   106 | # Define event; inputs: name. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   107 | def event\(name: str, **safe_fields: Any\) -> None:) Tj T*
(   108 |     # Call log.info to perform this step.) Tj T*
(   109 |     log.info\(json.dumps\({'event':name, 'ts':time.time\(\), **safe_fields},default=str\)\)) Tj T*
(   110 |) Tj T*
(   111 | @contextlib.contextmanager) Tj T*
(   112 | # Define span; inputs: name, trace_id. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   113 | def span\(name: str, trace_id: str\):) Tj T*
(   114 |     # Store time.perf_counter\(\) in start.) Tj T*
(   115 |     start=time.perf_counter\(\)) Tj T*
(   116 |     # Attempt this operation; handle errors or cleanup in the following clauses.) Tj T*
(   117 |     try:) Tj T*
(   118 |          yield) Tj T*
(   119 |          # Call event to perform this step.) Tj T*
(   120 |          event\('span_ok',span=name,trace_id=trace_id,ms=round\(\(time.perf_counter\(\)-start\)*1000\)\)) Tj T*
(   121 |     except Exception as exc:) Tj T*
(   122 |          # Call event to perform this step.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(   123 |         event\('span_failed',span=name,trace_id=trace_id,error_type=type\(exc\).__name__\)) Tj T*
(   124 |         # Stop normal execution and propagate an error to the caller.) Tj T*
(   125 |         raise) Tj T*
(   126 |) Tj T*
(   127 | # ----- 02 Real SQL storage: use parameterized queries and transactional writes.) Tj T*
(   128 | # Define db; inputs: none. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
