( 05 / PDF extraction, chunking, embeddings) Tj T*
( and ingestion) Tj T*
( What, why and how) Tj T*
( extract_pdf validates the file and yields page numbers and extracted text using pypdf. Scanned) Tj T*
( images need OCR, which is absent. chunks normalizes whitespace and slices text with step = size -) Tj T*
( overlap. embed lazily loads SentenceTransformer and encodes normalized vectors.) Tj T*
( all-MiniLM-L6-v2 produces 384 dimensions. ingest hashes file bytes, builds chunk metadata,) Tj T*
( embeds batches and inserts with duplicate protection.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Practical learning) Tj T*
( With size 1100 and overlap 180, step is 920; a 10,000-character normalized document produces 11) Tj T*
( chunks under this algorithm. Overlap preserves context but increases duplication. Cosine similarity) Tj T*
( = dot product / product of vector norms. Try a second upload and inspect duplicate handling.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Original source | lines 240-310) Tj T*
(   240 | def extract_pdf\(path: str\):) Tj T*
(   241 |     # Import dependencies used by the following code.) Tj T*
(   242 |     from pypdf import PdfReader) Tj T*
(   243 |     # Check not Path\(path\).is_file\(\) or Path\(path\).suffix.lower\(\) != '.pdf'; execute this branch only if) Tj T*
(       | true.) Tj T*
(   244 |     if not Path\(path\).is_file\(\) or Path\(path\).suffix.lower\(\)!='.pdf': raise ValueError\('PDF required'\)) Tj T*
(   245 |     # Check Path\(path\).stat\(\).st_size > 15000000; execute this branch only if true.) Tj T*
(   246 |     if Path\(path\).stat\(\).st_size>15_000_000: raise ValueError\('file too large'\)) Tj T*
(   247 |     # Production: antivirus, MIME/magic verification, decompression limits, OCR and document ACLs.) Tj T*
(   248 |     # Process each \(page_num, page\) from enumerate\(PdfReader\(path\).pages, 1\).) Tj T*
(   249 |     for page_num,page in enumerate\(PdfReader\(path\).pages,1\):) Tj T*
(   250 |         yield page_num,page.extract_text\(\) or '') Tj T*
(   251 |) Tj T*
(   252 | # Define chunks; inputs: text, size, overlap. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   253 | def chunks\(text: str,size: int=1100,overlap: int=180\):) Tj T*
(   254 |     # Check size <= overlap or overlap < 0; execute this branch only if true.) Tj T*
(   255 |     if size<=overlap or overlap<0: raise ValueError\('chunk size must exceed overlap'\)) Tj T*
(   256 |     # Store re.sub\('\\\\s+', ' ', text\).strip\(\) in text.) Tj T*
(   257 |     text=re.sub\(r'\\s+',' ',text\).strip\(\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(   258 |     # Store size - overlap in step.) Tj T*
(   259 |     step=size-overlap) Tj T*
(   260 |     # Return [text[i:i + size] for i in range\(0, len\(text\), step\) if text[i:i + size].strip\(\)] to the) Tj T*
(       | caller.) Tj T*
(   261 |     return [text[i:i+size] for i in range\(0,len\(text\),step\) if text[i:i+size].strip\(\)]) Tj T*
(   262 |) Tj T*
(   263 | # Store None in _embedding.) Tj T*
(   264 | _embedding=None) Tj T*
(   265 | # Store None in _reranker.) Tj T*
(   266 | _reranker=None) Tj T*
(   267 | # Define embed; inputs: texts. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   268 | def embed\(texts: list[str]\):) Tj T*
(   269 |     global _embedding) Tj T*
(   270 |     # Import dependencies used by the following code.) Tj T*
(   271 |     from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer) Tj T*
(   272 |     # Check _embedding is None; execute this branch only if true.) Tj T*
(   273 |     if _embedding is None: _embedding=SentenceTransformer\(C.embedding_model\)) Tj T*
(   274 |     # Return _embedding.encode\(texts, normalize_embeddings=True\).tolist\(\) to the caller.) Tj T*
(   275 |     return _embedding.encode\(texts,normalize_embeddings=True\).tolist\(\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(   276 |) Tj T*
(   277 | # Define ingest; inputs: path, tenant, actor. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   278 | def ingest\(path: str,tenant: str,actor: str\):) Tj T*
