( 07 / Retry and circuit breaker) Tj T*
( What, why and how) Tj T*
( CircuitOpen signals blocked dependency calls. CircuitBreaker tracks failures and recovery timing.) Tj T*
( retry repeats an operation with bounded attempts and delay. Retry handles transient errors; a) Tj T*
( circuit breaker stops repeated calls to an unhealthy service. Closed allows calls, open blocks,) Tj T*
( half-open conceptually probes recovery. Production requires explicit error classification, jitter,) Tj T*
( deadlines and concurrency controls.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Practical learning) Tj T*
( Simulate three failures, then a cooldown and successful recovery. Retry temporary timeouts and) Tj T*
( 503 responses; respect 429 Retry-After; do not blindly retry 401, 403 or invalid input.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Original source | lines 361-403) Tj T*
(   361 | class CircuitOpen\(RuntimeError\): pass) Tj T*
(   362 | # Define CircuitBreaker to group related state and behavior.) Tj T*
(   363 | class CircuitBreaker:) Tj T*
(   364 |     # Define __init__; inputs: self, threshold, reset_seconds. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   365 |     def __init__\(self,threshold=3,reset_seconds=40\):) Tj T*
(   366 |         # Store 0 in self.failures.) Tj T*
(   367 |         self.failures=0; self.opened_at=None) Tj T*
(   368 |         # Store threshold in self.threshold.) Tj T*
(   369 |         self.threshold=threshold; self.reset_seconds=reset_seconds) Tj T*
(   370 |     # Define call; inputs: self, fn. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   371 |     def call\(self,fn\):) Tj T*
(   372 |         # Check self.opened_at is not None; execute this branch only if true.) Tj T*
(   373 |         if self.opened_at is not None:) Tj T*
(   374 |             # Check time.monotonic\(\) - self.opened_at < self.reset_seconds; execute this branch only if) Tj T*
(       | true.) Tj T*
(   375 |             if time.monotonic\(\)-self.opened_at<self.reset_seconds: raise CircuitOpen\('model circuit) Tj T*
(       | open'\)) Tj T*
(   376 |             # Store None in self.opened_at.) Tj T*
(   377 |             self.opened_at=None; self.failures=0 # simple half-open probe; not concurrency-safe) Tj T*
(   378 |         # Attempt this operation; handle errors or cleanup in the following clauses.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(   379 |         try:) Tj T*
(   380 |              # Store fn\(\) in result.) Tj T*
(   381 |              result=fn\(\); self.failures=0; return result) Tj T*
(   382 |         except Exception:) Tj T*
(   383 |              self.failures+=1) Tj T*
(   384 |              # Check self.failures >= self.threshold; execute this branch only if true.) Tj T*
(   385 |              if self.failures>=self.threshold: self.opened_at=time.monotonic\(\)) Tj T*
(   386 |              # Stop normal execution and propagate an error to the caller.) Tj T*
(   387 |              raise) Tj T*
(   388 |) Tj T*
(   389 | # Store CircuitBreaker\(C.circuit_failures, C.circuit_reset_seconds\) in BREAKER.) Tj T*
(   390 | BREAKER=CircuitBreaker\(C.circuit_failures,C.circuit_reset_seconds\)) Tj T*
(   391 | # Define retry; inputs: fn, attempts. The body runs only when called.) Tj T*
(   392 | def retry\(fn,attempts=3\):) Tj T*
(   393 |     # Process each attempt from range\(attempts\).) Tj T*
(   394 |     for attempt in range\(attempts\):) Tj T*
(   395 |         # Attempt this operation; handle errors or cleanup in the following clauses.) Tj T*
(   396 |         try: return BREAKER.call\(fn\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
