( 09 / Checkpoints, DLQ and legacy graph) Tj T*
( What, why and how) Tj T*
( checkpoint persists workflow state; enqueue_failure stores failure information; workflow_id_for) Tj T*
( derives a stable ID. build_graph and _legacy_ask_reference are older reference paths. A checkpoint) Tj T*
( records progress, but safe resumption also needs idempotency. DLQ preserves failures for) Tj T*
( controlled investigation. QualityGateError and WorkflowCancelled distinguish failure categories.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Practical learning) Tj T*
( Submit the same request ID twice. Completed-result reuse is not atomic multi-worker idempotency.) Tj T*
( Avoid blindly replaying security failures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
