( 13 / Evaluation and LLM-as-a-Judge) Tj T*
( What, why and how) Tj T*
( evaluate uses basic expected-text checks and optional retrieval hits. llm_judge prompts a model to) Tj T*
( score grounding, parses JSON and validates the score range 0-5. Judges can be biased or wrong;) Tj T*
( calibrate with human-reviewed examples. Precision@K = relevant retrieved / K; recall@K =) Tj T*
( relevant retrieved / all known relevant; reciprocal rank = 1 / first relevant rank; MRR averages) Tj T*
( reciprocal ranks; nDCG measures ranking quality. Not all metrics are implemented.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Practical learning) Tj T*
( If ranks 1, 3 and 5 are relevant and five relevant documents exist, precision@5=60%,) Tj T*
( recall@5=60%, reciprocal rank=1, hit@5=1. Compare a generated answer of 20 leaves with) Tj T*
( evidence of 12.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
